From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:51:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Intercept sigaction on x86_64 guests

The host side registers guest handlers with the host signal chain
instead of the kernel, so the host runtime keeps its claimed signals.
bionic's sigaction.o defines only these two names, so with both
stubbed the archive member is never linked and bionic needs no change.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: the stub list is part of the x86_64 guest support this series adds; bionic's own sigaction is a raw rt_sigaction the launcher, loader or environment cannot route
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 android_api/libc/stubs_x86_64.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/android_api/libc/stubs_x86_64.cpp b/android_api/libc/stubs_x86_64.cpp
index 522c80eefe68ba664fbb877d0f9bf9233fa92506..3a01322a792d5ca89e85b01d0e08659aec221e3d 100644
--- a/android_api/libc/stubs_x86_64.cpp
+++ b/android_api/libc/stubs_x86_64.cpp
@@ -113,6 +113,8 @@ DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(pthread_setschedparam);
 DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(pthread_setschedprio);
 DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(pthread_setspecific);
 DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(pthread_sigqueue);
+DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(sigaction);
+DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(sigaction64);
 DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION(time);
 DEFINE_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_VARIABLE(environ);
 
@@ -209,6 +211,8 @@ static void __attribute__((constructor(0))) init_stub_library() {
   INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION("libc.so", pthread_setschedprio);
   INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION("libc.so", pthread_setspecific);
   INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION("libc.so", pthread_sigqueue);
+  INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION("libc.so", sigaction);
+  INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION("libc.so", sigaction64);
   INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_FUNCTION("libc.so", time);
   INIT_INTERCEPTABLE_STUB_VARIABLE("libc.so", environ);
 }
